[Music]  hey everyone  scott mccartney here 2020 wasn't a  normal year for travel  or anything air travel hasn't been this  disrupted  since 9 11 and the pandemic has been  much worse  but like every other year planes still  got stuck on the tarmac for hours  arrived late to their destinations and  bags still got lost  we've dug into loads of data that all  airlines tracked  and compiled rankings in seven  categories  for the best and worst major u.s  airlines of the year  let's start with formal complaints okay  here we go this is what really mattered  to consumers last year  in the study period there were more than  97  000 complaints filed at the department  of transportation  that's only a small part of angry  customers that actually  take the trouble to file a complaint  formally  but a year earlier there were only 15  000 complaints  more than 83 000 of those ninety seven  thousand complaints  were about refunds refund complaints  increased more than five thousand  percent  united and frontier were the big  offenders  both of them changed rules during the  pandemic and both made it really  difficult for customers to get refunds  that they were owed  remember when an airline cancels a  flight you are supposed to be entitled  to the option of a refund next  reliability which airlines are better at  getting you where you want to go  this category is on time arrivals the  industry  average for on-time arrivals was 84  of scheduled flights in 2019  the average was 79 5 points lower  delta was darn good at 87  and even with the skies open a legion  could only get  73 of its flights to the gate on time  next tarmac delays we look at  two hour tarmac delays that's kind of  the pain threshold for passengers stuck  in a cabin right  the numbers were small this year but  still there was significant variation  southwest had only 42 flights that sat  on the ground for two hours  with passengers aboard delta had 206.  next category mishandled baggage  [Music]  here some of the improvement came from  airlines in their systems  not from lighter loads southwest started  scanning bags  and monitoring the health of airport  baggage systems  and moved up to number two southwest had  the best improvement  americans rate of miss sandal bags was  down 24 percent  that's good but that wasn't nearly  enough to get it out of the baggage  seller  extreme delays this category is flights  delayed 45 minutes or more you're not  necessarily sitting on the airplane  but you are inconvenienced in other  words when things go wrong  they go bad wrong and there's wide  variation among airlines  only two percent of southwest flights  fell into this category  but eight percent of allegiant flights  canceled flights cancellations were huge  this past year right  but the department of transportation  says a flight is canceled if it's  scrubbed within seven days of departure  before that it's considered a schedule  change  so a lot of pandemic impact came in  schedule changes  the industry officially canceled six  percent of its flights in 2020 that's a  big number  especially compared to less than two  percent of the flights that were  canceled in 2019  involuntary bumping okay  so with few people flying how could  airlines possibly overbook flights  and involuntary bump passengers they did  all pandemic long not as many of course  but still hundreds of people delta  however  bumped only five passengers in the 12  months covered by the study  it got tens of thousands of passengers  to voluntarily change their flights  delta offered sweet incentives to do  that american by contrast  but more than 5 000 american actually  accounted for 77  of all u.s airline bumping over the last  12 months  the overall winner in airline  performance last year  southwest southwest was just  consistently good  at the top in most categories the one  exception was cancellations  it took southwest longer than other  airlines to publish  new schedules so it canceled a lot of  flights close to departure  but otherwise consistently good service  at southwest  and very few complaints the overall  loser  american again american has been last  or next to last in 12 of the 13 years  we've done the scorecard american had  trouble with long delays  baggage handling and bumping passengers  american wasn't very punctual compared  to others there was no category  where american airlines was any better  than the middle of the pack  pandemic or no american has work to do  to become a more reliable airline  don't you long for the days when you got  delayed because there were so many  planes trying to go somewhere  next year maybe worse airline  performance will really be a good thing

